#* {{quote-book|en|author=David Shields|title=Remote: Reflections on Life in the Shadow of Celebrity|year=2003|publisher=Univ of Wisconsin Press|page=49|pageurl=https://books.google.com/books?id=SCdih1A7l40C&pg=PA49&dq=%22sportscaster%22&hl=en&cd=34&source=gbs_api#v=onepage&q=%22sportscaster%22&f=false|isbn=978-0-299-19363-8|passage= At the beginning of the all-star game, the '''sportscaster''' always says that the players just want to have fun today; at halftime, or in the bottom of the fifth inning, the '''sportscaster''' always says that the players' competitive spirit has taken over and now they all really want to win.}}
# A person who comments on, presents, and reports sport events.

